# Local Test Timestamp Reporting

When the user asks to run a local test or local invoke, always include timestamps in the result summary.

Report, when available:
1. Start timestamp from runtime logs.
2. End/report timestamp or duration from runtime logs.
3. Any function-level timestamps in the returned payload (for example `checked_at`, `last_incoming_at`, `last_outgoing_at`).

If a timestamp is unavailable, explicitly say it was not present in output.
